---
import PageShell from '../../components/PageShell.astro';
import { MODELS, PROVIDERS } from '../../scripts/models.js';

const title = 'AI Context Window Comparison — 51 Models Ranked (2026)';
const description =
  'Compare context window sizes for 51 AI models: GPT-4o, Claude, Gemini, Llama & DeepSeek. See what fits at each size: words, pages and code files.';

const published = '2026-08-21T00:00:00Z';

const rows = Object.values(MODELS)
  .sort((a, b) => b.contextWindow - a.contextWindow);

const fmtCtx = (n) => (n >= 1_000_000 ? `${(n / 1_000_000).toFixed(n % 1_000_000 === 0 ? 0 : 1)}M` : `${Math.round(n / 1000)}K`);
const approxWords = (n) => Math.round(n * 0.75);
const approxPages = (n) => Math.round(approxWords(n) / 500);

const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'Which AI model has the largest context window?',
    a: 'Gemini-class models lead with context windows of 1 million tokens and beyond — enough for roughly 750,000 words or 1,500 pages in a single request. Most frontier models from OpenAI and Anthropic sit between 128K and 200K tokens.'
  },
  {
    q: 'How many words is a 128K context window?',
    a: 'About 96,000 English words (~4 characters per token, 0.75 words per token) — roughly 190 pages of prose, a small codebase, or about 480 chat messages of 200 words each.'
  },
  {
    q: 'Does a bigger context window cost more?',
    a: 'Usually yes. Some providers charge more per token above certain context thresholds, and long prompts always cost proportionally more because you pay per token regardless of window size. Filling a 1M-token window is far pricier than filling 8K.'
  },
  {
    q: 'Do models actually use their full context well?',
    a: 'Not always. Effective recall degrades in the middle of very long contexts ("lost in the middle" effect). Best practice: keep critical instructions near the beginning or end of the prompt, even when the window is huge.'
  }
];
---

<PageShell
  title={title}
  description={description}
  path="/guides/context-window-comparison/"
  type="article"
  publishedTime={published}
  modifiedTime={published}
  eyebrow="Guide · Reference"
  heading="Context Window Comparison: 51 AI Models Ranked"
  lead="The context window is how much text a model can consider at once — your prompt, documents and the reply all share it. Here is every supported model, largest first, with what fits inside."
  faqs={faqs}
  faqTitle="Context window FAQ"
>
  <article class="prose">
    <div class="table-card">
      <table class="pricing">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Model</th>
            <th scope="col">Provider</th>
            <th scope="col">Context</th>
            <th scope="col">≈ Words</th>
            <th scope="col">≈ Pages</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {rows.map((m) => (
            <tr>
              <td><span class="model-name">{m.name}</span></td>
              <td>{PROVIDERS[m.provider].name}</td>
              <td class="num">{fmtCtx(m.contextWindow)} tokens</td>
              <td class="num">{approxWords(m.contextWindow).toLocaleString()}</td>
              <td class="num">{approxPages(m.contextWindow).toLocaleString()}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h2>What actually fits in a context window</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>8K tokens</strong> — ~6,000 words: a long essay or a handful of chat turns.</li>
      <li><strong>32K tokens</strong> — ~24,000 words: a novella, a product spec, a day of logs.</li>
      <li><strong>128K tokens</strong> — ~96,000 words: a small book or an entire mid-size codebase.</li>
      <li><strong>200K+ tokens</strong> — ~150,000 words: multi-document research packs.</li>
      <li><strong>1M+ tokens</strong> — ~750,000 words: whole repositories, hour-long transcripts, video analysis.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Three practical notes</h2>
    <p>
      First, <strong>the window is shared</strong>: input + output must fit together, so a
      128K model with a 30K prompt leaves ~98K minus any reserved output cap.
      Second, some providers apply <strong>tiered pricing above a threshold</strong> — the
      same token can cost more as your conversation grows. Third, bigger windows invite
      bigger prompts; pair them with
      <a href="/guides/prompt-caching/">prompt caching</a> so repeated prefixes stay cheap,
      and estimate real workloads in the <a href="/">calculator's Chat tab</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</PageShell>
